            <ArticleTitle>A comparison between propranolol and hypothermia in preventing ischemic contracture of the left ventricle (stone heart).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>541-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ischemic contracture of the left ventricle (&quot;stone heart&quot;) was studied utilizing a previously described stone heart model. Our studies suggest that beta-adrenergic blockade is not quantitatively as important as hypothermia in protecting ischemic myocardium. On the basis of reduced fibrillatory activity and a slight protective effect shown by electron microscopy, it would appear that combining propranolol with hypothermia may be superior to either used singly.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
